      "body": "## Description\r\nThis PR updates the streaming logic in `serving.py` to handle engine outputs marked with `FINISHED_ABORTED`.\r\n\r\nWhen an engine request is aborted mid-stream, vLLM will now:\r\n1. Emit an error event payload to inform the client.\r\n2. Skip emitting the final `data: [DONE]` terminal signal.\r\n\r\n## Motivation\r\nPreviously, when an engine request transitioned into `FINISHED_ABORTED`, the streaming pipeline could still emit `data: [DONE]`. This caused OpenAI-compatible clients to treat the request as a successful completion even though the generation was canceled or interrupted mid-stream.\r\n\r\n## Testing Executed\r\n- Verified unit test coverage using `pytest tests/entrypoints/openai/responses/test_streaming_events.py` (7 passed).\r\n- Confirmed with a standalone verification test that `FINISHED_ABORTED` states emit the error event without appending the `[DONE]` signal.\r\n\r\n## AI Disclosure\r\nThis PR was developed with assistance from Gemini for debugging environment dependencies and verifying streaming logic assertions.\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n- [x] Commits are signed off with `-s` (DCO).\r\n- [x] PR title follows `[Type][Scope]` conventions.\r\n- [x] Changes were tested locally.",
